  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message as the implied subject of the metaphor",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material (text_chunk_1) which presents a hypothetical scenario ('if you hold a person underwater...') that implicitly addresses the user as the potential actor performing the action. The meme's structure invites the user to imagine themselves as the one holding someone underwater, thereby projecting the user's identity onto the textual command and its implied action. This projection is not explicit with 'you' or 'me' but is implied through the imperative tone and the universalizing nature of the statement, making the user the assumed agent of the action described.",
